1
00:00:00,620 --> 00:00:07,840
Example 1: Set up then calculate.

2
00:00:07,840 --> 00:00:18,400
56 times 23

3
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:25,640
Perform calculation and set up as follows:

4
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:31,930
Set up vertically.

5
00:00:31,930 --> 00:00:37,970
Find first partial product.

6
00:00:37,970 --> 00:00:46,040
3 times 6 equals 18, write 8 carry 1

7
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:59,840
3 times 5 equals 15, plus 1 equals 16, write 16

8
00:01:01,150 --> 00:01:07,350
Find second partial product

9
00:01:07,350 --> 00:01:16,440
2 times 6 equals 12, write 2 carry 1

10
00:01:16,440 --> 00:01:27,310
2 times 5 equals 10, plus 1 equals 11, write 11

11
00:01:27,710 --> 00:01:36,370
Second partial product shifted left by 1 place.

12
00:01:36,370 --> 00:01:47,280
Add 2 partial products we get 1288

13
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:55,000
Example 2: Set up then calculate.

14
00:01:55,530 --> 00:02:04,280
Calculate 65 times 37

15
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:13,370
Set up multiplication like multiplying by a one-digit number.

16
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:19,800
Find first partial product.

17
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:26,370
Find second partial product

18
00:02:26,640 --> 00:02:35,370
Add 2 partial products we get result.

19
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:41,170
First partial product.

20
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:52,200
7 times 65 equals 455

21
00:02:52,860 --> 00:03:01,530
Second partial product set below first partial product and shifted one place because 3 is tens place.

22
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:10,680
3 times 65 equals 195

23
00:03:11,220 --> 00:03:23,330
Adding two partial products we get 2405

24
00:03:24,170 --> 00:03:37,110
Lesson end: When multiplying by a two-digit number we set up like multiplying by one-digit number then perform 3 steps calculation.

25
00:03:37,110 --> 00:03:39,550
Find first partial product.

26
00:03:39,550 --> 00:03:46,330
Find second partial product set below first partial product (shifted left one place).

27
00:03:46,330 --> 00:03:52,150
Find sum of 2 partial products.

